<title>USA: BPA offers no peak, firm power for Wed-Thurs.</title>
<headline>BPA offers no peak, firm power for Wed-Thurs.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bonneville Power Administration (BPA) offerd no peak firm power for Wednesday and Thursday pre-schedulings, the agency said Monday ahead of a three-day training seminar.</p>
<p>On Monday, BPA had offered an unlimited volume of light-load firm power for both days at $9.00 for both the Northwest and California-Oregon border (COB) deliveries.</p>
<p>BPA prices for non-firm power during hours ending 0100-0500 and 2400 PDT were also unchanged at $7.00 for Northwest and $8.00 at COB.</p>
<p>Non-firm power during hours ending 0600, 0700 and 2300 PDT was unchanged at $10.00.</p>
<p>((--Los Angeles bureau +1 213 955 6761))</p>
